# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon: experimental compact span encoding (CHARON_COMPACT_SPANS=1)
#
# Spans take a quarter of large LLBC files: every span is written as
# {"data":{"file_id":..,"beg":{"line":..,"col":..},"end":{..}},"generated_from_span":..}.
# With CHARON_COMPACT_SPANS=1 the exporter writes [file, beg_line, beg_col,
# end_line, end_col], followed by five more numbers when generated_from_span is
# present (chelis-deep: 187.6 MB -> 150.0 MB). The default format is unchanged and
# charon-ml cannot read the compact one, so this is a measurement prototype only.
# Charon's own deserializer accepts both encodings (compact_spans_round_trip).
#
# Span implements the stateless serde_state traits by hand because the
# serde_state derive does not accept serde(into/from).

